This is exactly why we do a "Frontend Audit" before dropping a database column! You made the right call by checking these files.
I have reviewed all three files. **Yes, your frontend is still using the payload column**, specifically in the **JournalRequestApproval.js** file. If you dropped the column from Oracle today, the "View Details" modal on the approval screen would completely crash.
Here is the exact breakdown of what I found in your code:
### 1. The Culprit: JournalRequestApproval.js
In the fetchBatchDetailsPaginated function, I can see that you (or another developer) already started the migration. You are correctly mapping the new, optimized database columns:
```javascript
